('JEE Main','Physics','Kinematics','easy','A car starts from rest and accelerates uniformly at 4 m/s² for 5 s. The distance covered is:','["50 m","25 m","100 m","40 m"]',0,'s = ½at² = ½×4×25 = 50 m.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('JEE Main','Physics','Kinematics','medium','A projectile is launched at 45° with speed 20 m/s. The horizontal range (g=10 m/s²) is:','["40 m","20 m","10 m","80 m"]',0,'R = u²sin2θ/g = 400×1/10 = 40 m.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('JEE Main','Physics','Kinematics','hard','Two stones are thrown vertically upward simultaneously with speeds 20 m/s and 25 m/s from the same point. After 2 s the distance between them is:','["10 m","15 m","8 m","12 m"]',0,'Stone1: 20×2−5×4=20 m; Stone2: 25×2−5×4=30 m. Difference = 10 m.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('JEE Main','Physics','Laws of Motion','medium','A 2 kg block on a frictionless surface is pushed by a 10 N force. Acceleration is:','["5 m/s²","10 m/s²","2 m/s²","20 m/s²"]',0,'a = F/m = 10/2 = 5 m/s².','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('JEE Main','Physics','Laws of Motion','hard','A 60 kg man stands in a lift. Normal force when lift accelerates downward at 2 m/s² (g=10):','["480 N","600 N","720 N","400 N"]',0,'N = m(g−a) = 60×8 = 480 N.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('JEE Main','Physics','Work Energy Power','medium','A 5 kg body moves from rest with constant force 20 N for 4 s. Work done is:','["640 J","320 J","160 J","80 J"]',0,'a=4 m/s², v=16 m/s, s=32 m, W=Fs=20×32=640 J.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('JEE Main','Physics','Work Energy Power','hard','A spring (k=500 N/m) is compressed 10 cm. If a 1 kg ball rests on it, its maximum height after release (g=10):','["0.25 m","0.5 m","1.0 m","2.0 m"]',0,'½kx²=mgh → h = 500×0.01/(2×1×10) = 0.25 m.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('JEE Main','Physics','Rotational Motion','medium','A solid cylinder (M=2 kg, R=0.5 m) rotates at 10 rad/s. Its rotational KE is:','["12.5 J","25 J","6.25 J","50 J"]',0,'I=½MR²=0.25 kg·m², KE=½Iω²=½×0.25×100=12.5 J.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('JEE Main','Physics','Rotational Motion','hard','A disc rolls without slipping at speed v. Ratio of rotational KE to total KE is:','["1/3","1/2","2/3","1/4"]',0,'KE_rot=½Iω²=¼Mv², KE_total=¾Mv², ratio=1/3.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('JEE Main','Physics','Gravitation','medium','The escape velocity from a planet of radius R and density ρ is proportional to:','["R√ρ","R/√ρ","√(Rρ)","ρ/R"]',0,'v_e=√(2GM/R); M∝ρR³ → v_e∝R√ρ.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('JEE Main','Physics','Gravitation','hard','A geostationary satellite orbits at radius 42000 km. A satellite at 6R_E has time period:','["8 h","16 h","24 h","12 h"]',0,'T∝r^(3/2). Using Kepler: T₁=24h at 42000km≈6.6R_E. At 6R_E slightly less. Approx 24h for geostationary by definition.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('JEE Main','Physics','Thermodynamics','easy','In an isothermal process for an ideal gas, which quantity remains constant?','["Temperature","Pressure","Volume","Internal energy change is zero"]',3,'For isothermal: T=const, but P and V can change; ΔU=0 for ideal gas.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('JEE Main','Physics','Thermodynamics','medium','1 mol ideal gas expands isothermally at 300 K from 1 L to 2 L. Work done (R=8.314):','["1729 J","1000 J","500 J","2500 J"]',0,'W=nRT ln(V₂/V₁)=1×8.314×300×0.693=1729 J.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('JEE Main','Physics','Thermodynamics','hard','A Carnot engine operates between 400 K and 300 K. Efficiency is:','["25%","33%","50%","75%"]',0,'η=1−T_L/T_H=1−300/400=0.25=25%.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('JEE Main','Physics','Waves','easy','The speed of sound in air at 0°C is 332 m/s. At 4°C it is approximately:','["333 m/s","330 m/s","340 m/s","332 m/s"]',0,'v∝√T; small change gives ~333 m/s.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('JEE Main','Physics','Waves','medium','Two waves y₁=A sin(ωt) and y₂=A sin(ωt+π) superpose. Resultant amplitude is:','["0","2A","A","A√2"]',0,'Phase difference=π → destructive interference → amplitude=0.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
